  "summary": "SF Democratic Party chair Nancy Tung blocked a resolution calling for restrictions on Flock Safety the same month she accepted a $10,000 donation from billionaire Chris Larsen, a major funder of SFPD's surveillance program, and spoke at a Flock conference in Atlanta. The article details her officeholder-account spending, Flock ties among other party board members, and a later party resolution lauding SF's use of ALPRs.",
  "key_quotes": [
    {
      "quote": "The same month she blocked a resolution calling for restrictions on Flock Safety, the chairperson of the San Francisco Democratic Party accepted a $10,000 donation from a tech mogul bankrolling the police department's surveillance deployment and spoke at a conference hosted by the firm.",
      "paragraph_idx": 6
    },
    {
      "quote": "A Standard investigation last year revealed that San Francisco's Flock license-plate database was illegally accessed 1.6 million times by out-of-state agencies.",
      "paragraph_idx": 20
    },
    {
      "quote": "Larsen has donated roughly $12 million in gifts to the San Francisco Police Department's surveillance efforts, helping beef up its Real-Time Investigation Center.",
      "paragraph_idx": 21
    }
  ],
